37. Rxg8 Kxg8 38. Qe6 Kf8 39. c4 { And the queen endgame is winning. } ) 
34. Qxd6 Qxd6 35. Rxd6 { Black has some drawing chances. } ) 
32. Ne6 Bf6 33. Qxb7 ( { An alternative is } 33. Nd8 $5 Qxf7 34. Nxf7 Kg8 35. Nxd6 { with a big advantage for White. } ) 
Rxb7 34. Rxd6 { White is a full pawn up. In addition, his knight is more useful than Black’s restricted dark-squared bishop, and the pawns on a5 and e5 are weak. Hence the advantage is nearly decisive. } Kg8 35. Ra6 Rb5 36. Rc6 { Planning to follow with Nc5-e4 with full control of the board. } Be7 $6 { Making things worse. } ( { Better was } 36... Rd5 { though White still has a huge advantage after } 37. Kf1 Kf7 38. Ke2 { . } ) 
